p2c. A sound, conservative, const-checkable predicate for the headroom axis.

Soundness here means: never predict UNOBSERVABLE where measurement finds
the axis observable. That is the direction a resolver acts on, so it is
the only direction whose error rate may be zero rather than small.

--- setting one: W = 4, containers 4 against 12, chain length 3

op         congruent   contracting   container-read 
wadd       true        false         false          
wsub       true        false         false          
wmul       true        false         false          
shr        false       true          false          
div        false       true          false          
sat_at_W   false       true          false          
sat_at_C   false       false         true           
min        false       true          false          
cmp        false       true          false          

